# regression.numos — Screenshot script for Regression app (RegressionApp, APP 06)
#
# Three shots required by the website (DELIVERABLES.md):
# 1. /assets/img/apps/regression-1.webp — Equation tab after a QUADRATIC fit:
#    equation, each coefficient, R2, point count.
# 2. /assets/img/apps/regression-2.webp — Graph tab: entered points as scatter
#    and the fitted curve passing through them.
# 3. /assets/img/apps/regression-3.webp — the same graph after switching the
#    model, the quadratic curve replaced by a straight line.
#
# ── App state machine (src/apps/RegressionApp.cpp) ──────────────────────
#   * begin()/load() build a 3-tab screen: Data (table X|Y), Equation, Graph.
#     load() resets _activeTab=DATA, tableRow=0, tableCol=0, _editing=false and
#     calls refreshTable() (RegressionApp.cpp:138-149). _model is set ONCE in the
#     constructor to LINEAR (RegressionApp.cpp:69) and is never persisted.
#   * Data tab nav (handleKeyData, :750-848): a DIGIT in nav mode starts an edit
#     and re-processes itself (startEdit + recurse, :842-845); ENTER commits
#     (finishEdit, :785-788); RIGHT/LEFT move between the X and Y columns (they
#     are column nav, NOT a tab switch, :810-821); AC appends a fresh row and
#     DOWN walks onto it (:831-838); DEL clears the focused cell; in edit mode
#     digits/DOT append, DEL backspaces, ENTER commits, AC cancels.
#   * startEdit() pre-fills the buffer with the cell's current value whenever the
#     row already holds data (:417-424). Every cell written below is either on a
#     freshly appended last row (x=0,y=0, row==_numRows-1 -> NO pre-fill) or a
#     Y cell whose pre-fill "0" is absorbed by atof ("011" == 11), so the
#     committed values are exactly the ones listed at the bottom.
#   * Tab switching when not editing: F1 = previous, F2 = next, GRAPH cycles
#     Data -> Equation -> Graph -> Data (:720-737). GRAPH is the only key that
#     leaves the Data tab. switchTab(EQUATION) runs recompute()+updateEquationDisplay();
#     switchTab(GRAPH) runs recompute()+updateGraph() (:334-348).
#
# ── Model toggle: UNREACHABLE in this build (why shots 1 and 3 are absent) ──
#   * RegressionApp toggles _model LINEAR<->QUADRATIC on KeyCode::SHIFT in the
#     Equation and Graph tab handlers ONLY (RegressionApp.cpp:854-877); the
#     Equation label literally says "(SHIFT to toggle)". There is no other key,
#     no other entry point and no persistence that can change _model.
#   * The emulator routes keys through NativeHal::dispatchKey(), which swallows
#     SHIFT on its DOWN edge for every mode that does not own its modifiers
#     (NativeHal.cpp:767-775: appOwnsModifiers = CALCULATION|CALCULUS|EQUATIONS|
#     GAMEBOY). REGRESSION is not in that list, so `key shift` sets the shared
#     KeyboardManager and RETURNs — RegressionApp::handleKey never sees it. The
#     trailing RELEASE does reach the app but is discarded by its own action
#     filter (RegressionApp.cpp:717 accepts only PRESS/REPEAT).
#   * PROVEN empirically on this binary, not just read: emitContextLineIfChanged()
#     prints "@ctx <id> <slug> <modifier>" at the end of every frame whenever the
#     modifier indicator changes, unconditionally (NativeHal.cpp:4246-4249). A
#     `key shift` inside Regression emits "@ctx 8 regression S" — the KeyboardManager
#     took the key — while the control `key shift` inside the Menu emits
#     "@ctx 1 menu S". If the app had received the key, no modifier line would
#     appear. (The same swallow exists on the device: SystemApp.cpp:782-787.)
#   * Therefore the model stays LINEAR for the whole run: shot 1 (a quadratic
#     fit) and shot 3 (a model switch) CANNOT be reached, and there is no
#     assertion anywhere that can read _model or any label text to prove a model
#     claim anyway. Both shots are reported COULD NOT CAPTURE rather than
#     photographed as the wrong screen.
#
# ── Dataset typed here (linear on purpose) ──────────────────────────────
#   (0,1) (1,3) (2,5) (3,7) (4,9) (5,11)   ->  n = 6, y = 2x + 1, R2 = 1
#   Lying exactly on a straight line means the LINEAR fit — the only model this
#   build can select — passes through every plotted point, which is what shot 2's
#   SHOW asks for. It also keeps x=0 and y=0 inside the auto-scaled ranges, so
#   updateGraph()->drawAxes() actually draws both axis lines (RegressionApp.cpp:611-636);
#   all-positive data would leave 0 outside the 15% margins and draw no axes at all.
#   Fitted values the Equation tab would carry (from RegressionEngine::fitLinear):
#   m = 2, b = 1, c = N/A, R2 = 1, n = 6 — derived from the engine, not observed.
#
# Theme: default is NumOS (ThemeManager ctor); Regression has no casio-specific
# code, so assert_theme numos holds with no toggle.
#
# NOTE: the script parser reads a whole token per command, so no inline '#'
# comments are allowed after key/wait/screenshot/assert — every comment sits
# on its own line.
#
# Run (from repo root):
#   ./C:/.piobuild/numOS/emulator_pc/program --headless --deterministic \
#       --script tests/emulator/scripts/screenshots/regression.numos \
#       --fs-root tests/emulator/fs --frames 1400 --quiet
# Exit codes: 0 ok · 2 script/parse error · 3 screenshot write error · 4 assertion failure.

log "regression: waiting for launcher"
wait 200
assert_app Menu
assert_theme numos

# Open Regression directly (emulator launchApp id 6, same id as the launcher card).
open_app Regression
wait 60
assert_app Regression
assert_theme numos

# ── Data entry: six rows ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Row 0: X=0, Y=1. Starts at row 0 / col 0 in nav mode; the first row is the
# only empty row, so both edits open with no pre-fill.
key 0
key enter
key right
key 1
key enter

# Row 1: back to the X column, append a row, walk down onto it, X=1, Y=3.
key left
key ac
key down
key 1
key enter
key right
key 3
key enter

# Row 2: X=2, Y=5.
key left
key ac
key down
key 2
key enter
key right
key 5
key enter

# Row 3: X=3, Y=7.
key left
key ac
key down
key 3
key enter
key right
key 7
key enter

# Row 4: X=4, Y=9.
key left
key ac
key down
key 4
key enter
key right
key 9
key enter

# Row 5: X=5, Y=11 (two digits; the Y pre-fill "0" yields "011" -> 11).
key left
key ac
key down
key 5
key enter
key right
key 1
key 1
key enter

# ── SHOT 1 target: Equation tab, quadratic fit — REACHED, NOT CAPTURED ──
# GRAPH cycles Data -> Equation, which recomputes and fills the six labels
# (equation, slope/a, intercept/b, c, R2, points). The site wants this tab AFTER
# A QUADRATIC FIT; the only key that changes the model is SHIFT and the emulator
# swallows it before the app (see header). Press it anyway so the run log carries
# the proof: "@ctx 8 regression S" right after this line means KeyboardManager
# took the key and the app did not.
key graph
wait 120
assert_app Regression
assert_theme numos
key shift
wait 5
assert_app Regression
log "regression: equation tab reached with 6 points; SHIFT swallowed (see @ctx line above), model still LINEAR -> shot 1 NOT captured"

# ── SHOT 2: Graph tab, scatter + fitted curve ──────────────────────────
# GRAPH cycles Equation -> Graph; switchTab(GRAPH) runs recompute()+updateGraph():
# 6 scatter dots, both axis lines (0 lies inside both auto-scaled ranges) and the
# least-squares line y = 2x + 1 drawn over them (RegressionApp.cpp:593-597).
key graph
wait 120
assert_app Regression
assert_theme numos
screenshot out/shots-regression-2.ppm
log "regression: shot 2 captured (graph tab: 6 points + fitted line y=2x+1)"

# ── SHOT 3 target: same graph with the model switched — NOT CAPTURED ───
# The site wants the quadratic curve replaced by a straight line here. That needs
# a second SHIFT (handleKeyGraph, RegressionApp.cpp:869-877); the same swallow
# blocks it, and no assertion can read _model, so there is nothing to capture and
# nothing to prove. Logged, not screenshotted — a second identical frame would
# ship as a false "after switching" picture.
assert_app Regression
assert_theme numos
log "regression: model switch not reachable (key shift is consumed by dispatchKey) -> shot 3 NOT captured"
log "regression: done"
